      <section id="how-it-works" class="section">
        <h2>How Bag-on-Valve Technology Works</h2>
        <p>The operating mechanism of a BOV aerosol system is based on simple volumetric displacement and mechanical compression. When the actuator is depressed, the valve channel opens to the atmosphere, creating a pressure differential between the inside of the laminated bag and the external nozzle orifice. The pressurized nitrogen surrounding the bag squeezes the flexible walls inward, forcing the liquid up and out of the nozzle. Because nitrogen behaves as an ideal gas, its physical properties can be analyzed using standard gas dynamics databases like the <a href="https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">PubChem</a> database.</p>
        <p>Because the propellant gas does not mix with the liquid, there is no pressure drop associated with gas dissolution. The product is discharged at a steady rate, maintaining consistent spray characteristics from the first spray until the container is completely empty. The table below compares the functional properties of BOV systems with conventional aerosol systems:</p>

